Cutthroat Rings	25	{"kind":"quest","title":"Cutthroat Rings","wikiPath":"/Cutthroat_Rings","sources":[{"kind":"quest","where":"West Commonlands","detail":"Start zone"},{"kind":"quest","where":"Guard Valon","detail":"Quest giver"}],"components":[{"name":"Orc Pawn Pick","qty":4,"wikiPath":"/Orc_Pawn_Pick"},{"name":"Cutthroat Insignia Ring","qty":1,"wikiPath":"/Cutthroat_Insignia_Ring"}],"rewards":[{"text":"Faction, Militia Armory Token"}],"card":{"title":"Cutthroat Rings","lines":["Minimum Level: 10","Classes: All","Related Zones: None","Related NPCs: a Dervish Cutthroat, a Dervish Thug","Faction note: This quest is given by Guard Valon at the toll booth in the Commonlands. You must have atleast Indifferent faction with the Freeport Militia in order to receive it."]},"links":["Ortallius' Cutthroat Rings","West Commonlands","Guard Valon","A Dervish Cutthroat","A Dervish Thug","Faction","Militia Armory Token","Orc Picks","Orc Pawn Pick","Bag for Cutthroat Rings","Cutthroat Insignia Ring","Coalition of Tradefolk Underground","Freeport Militia","Knights of Truth","Priests of Marr","Reserve Militia"],"fetchedAt":"2026-09-23T05:43:22.016Z","outOfEra":false}
Holy Armor Scroll	25	{"kind":"quest","title":"Holy Armor Scroll","wikiPath":"/Holy_Armor_Scroll","sources":[{"kind":"quest","where":"South Qeynos","detail":"Start zone"},{"kind":"quest","where":"Daedet Losaren","detail":"Quest giver"}],"components":[],"rewards":[{"text":"Spell: Holy Armor","item":"Holy Armor","wikiPath":"/Holy_Armor"}],"card":{"title":"Holy Armor Scroll","lines":["Minimum Level: 2","Classes: Cleric, Paladin","Related Zones: Erud's Crossing","Related NPCs: Kerra Isle beetle, a fire beetle","Faction note: Note: This quest requires indifferent or better faction."]},"links":["Qeynos","Daedet Losaren","Cleric","Paladin","Erud's Crossing","Kerra Isle beetle","A fire beetle","Holy Armor","Beetle Eye Chest","Kerra Isle Beetle eye","Fire Beetle Eye","Knights of Thunder","Bloodsabers","Priests of Life","Guards of Qeynos"],"dialogue":[{"npc":"Daedet Losaren","text":"Welcome Elrood. I am Deadet Losaren, faithful priest of Karana. You appear to be in search of [guidance] or perhaps you are merely a [visitor to the temple of thunder] wishing the blessing of [Holy Armor]."},{"npc":"Daedet Losaren","text":"Holy Armor? I offer good standing members of the Knights of Thunder the blessing of Holy Armor. I must charge ten gold for the service. [Components] are expensive these days."},{"npc":"Daedet Losaren","text":"Components are required for my daily tribute to the Rainkeeper. It is he whose power flows from my body. I require a faithful acolyte to [gather the required items]."},{"npc":"Daedet Losaren","text":"Very noble of you. Take this chest. I will require it to be filled with flame beetle eyes. Four normal beetles and four [Kerra Isle Beetles]. Combine these items within the chest and return it to me and I shall reward you with the power of Holy Armor."},{"npc":"Daedet Losaren","text":"Kerra Isle Beetles are within the territory of the Kerra Catpeople, but a closer and perhaps safer location would be on the island between Antonica and Odus. The outcast Catpeople of that island are far less dangerous."},{"npc":"Daedet Losaren","text":"You have done well. Karana is pleased. I cannot say the same for the cat people. I reward you this. It is not much, but may be of use while you serve our wills."}],"fetchedAt":"2026-09-23T05:43:23.101Z","outOfEra":false}
Lenka's Pouch	25	{"kind":"quest","title":"Lenka's Pouch","wikiPath":"/Lenka's_Pouch","sources":[{"kind":"quest","where":"West Freeport","detail":"Start zone"},{"kind":"quest","where":"Toala Nehron","detail":"Quest giver"}],"components":[],"rewards":[{"text":"Moggok's Right Eye","item":"Moggok's Right Eye","wikiPath":"/Moggok%27s_Right_Eye"},{"text":"Snapped Pole","item":"Snapped Pole","wikiPath":"/Snapped_Pole"},{"text":"Fishing Pole","item":"Fishing Pole","wikiPath":"/Fishing_Pole"}],"card":{"title":"Lenka's Pouch","lines":["Minimum Level: 1","Classes: ?","Related Zones: East Freeport","Related NPCs: Brunar Rankin, Lenka Stoutheart, Olunea Miltin, Bronto Thudfoot"]},"links":["Freeport","Toala Nehron","East Freeport","Brunar Rankin","Lenka Stoutheart","Olunea Miltin","Bronto Thudfoot","Moggok's Right Eye","Snapped Pole","Fishing Pole","West Freeport","L.S. Pouch","Wolves of the North","Shamen of Justice","Merchants of Halas","Steel Warriors","Freeport Militia","Coalition of Tradefolk Ill","Knights of Truth","Priests of Marr"],"dialogue":[{"npc":"Toala Nehron","text":"I am Toala Nehron. You must be another young warrior aspiring to join the ranks of the Steel Warriors. We welcome all who would try. When you [have time], there is a friend of mine I would like you to check on."},{"npc":"Toala Nehron","text":"I have a friend by the name of [Lenka Stoutheart]. She reported to me that her ship was broken into and someone stole a pouch of hers. Could you go look into it for me? Just tell her Toala sent you. Oh, and pay no mind to the walking mountain by her. That will only be Bronto, her navigator. Thanks, friend."},{"npc":"Toala Nehron","text":"Lenka Stoutheart is an old friend of mine. I trained with her in my younger days when the Steel Warriors sent me to train in the ways of the Wolves of the North, the barbarian warriors of Halas. She is now an adventurer of great sorts. She travels from continent to continent aboard the Blue Beast, her ship. The Last time I had heard from her she was docked in East Karana."},{"npc":"Lenka Stoutheart","text":"Hi, kid! You seem to be a stranger in these parts. Heed my words, this city is dangerous to new blood!"},{"npc":"Bronto Thudfoot","text":"You said it, boss! Stay clear of taking sides and you should be just fine, young one ."},{"npc":"Lenka Stoutheart","text":"She does not even have the courtesy to come herself. Some old friend!! Listen, some rogue in this city broke into the [Beast] and stole a pouch containing a voucher ticket for a part I need to repair the Beast. I can't get the part back without the ticket. I did not see the rogue. I did not sleep on the Beast that night. Bronto was there. Ask him if he saw the rogue."},{"npc":"Lenka Stoutheart","text":"You're joking, right? You have never heard of the Blue Beast?!! She is the fastest ship in Norrath. She made the [Kunark run] in under three weeks. She was designed by [Bronto]."},{"npc":"Lenka Stoutheart","text":"The Kunark run is the most dangerous run between Freeport and [Firiona Vie], in Kunark. If the seas don't rip your hull to splinters and the pirates and sea wyrms don't kill you, you can make a quick run back and forth, avoiding any unwanted inspections."},{"npc":"Lenka Stoutheart","text":"Firiona Vie is an elven outpost on the continent of Kunark. Every so often I run supplies to and from there. Do not even think about asking me to take you there. It will be months before I can make improvements on the Blue Beast to make it impervious to aerial attacks."},{"npc":"Bronto Thudfoot","text":"I had quite a bit of grog that night and it was very dark. What I do remember was seeing a tall woman in a dress run from the docks. She sort of smelled, too. Like fish. I know it was the docks, but this woman had a real stench to her. Like dried fish baking in the sun. That is all I remember. It was too dark to see anything but her [silhouette]."},{"npc":"Bronto Thudfoot","text":"Yeah!! The silhouette looked like a very brawny woman. It had to be a woman. The silhouette was surely that of one with a short skirt and long hair."},{"npc":"Brunar Rankin","text":"How are you? Please excuse my stench. I fish all day and night just to feed my large family. You look like an adventurer. That must be exciting. I am but a humble fisherman. Maybe someday we shall both be rich. You by your treasures and me by my catch."},{"npc":"Brunar Rankin","text":"How dare you accuse me of being a thief!? I labor hour after hour trying to catch one fish which will bring me one copper piece to buy one slice of bread which I will split into five pieces to feed me, my sick wife and three little children, one of whom has the plague!! Poor little Repi. Now please, leave this humble little fisherman alone!"},{"npc":"Oliunea Miltin","text":"Great !! Thank you stranger. The rogues must have broken it. At least I can repair it. It would be seasons before I could afford another pole."}],"fetchedAt":"2026-09-23T05:43:24.180Z","outOfEra":false}
